--- body ---
Parent: 1444

## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: use the existing stdlib policy; dependency inspection belongs to harness-doctor. No new rules. Existing policy distinguishes bundled helpers from harness tools whose dependencies come from the lock.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A reusable on-demand harness-doctor dependency diagnostic identifies the applicable policy/perimeter and reports direct stdlib, local, and third-party import candidates with prerequisites and evidence limits.
- [ ] A positive control detects a third-party import; stdlib/local controls avoid false findings. Dynamic imports and unexamined transitive/runtime requirements are reported as limitations or unavailable, never a clean dependency bill.
- [ ] Reuse existing import/source infrastructure where practical; any helper is stdlib and an instrument, not a gate. Demonstrate bounded use without a forced workflow migration or new exception registry.
- [ ] No new general rule, routine healthcheck, scheduled sweep, or merge-gate integration. Run checks appropriate to changed behavior.
